# Next.js .env.development — loaded automatically when NODE_ENV=development.
# Committed to the repo; this file holds NON-SECRET defaults only.
# Secret values (API keys, service-role keys) go in .env.local (gitignored).
#
# AI feature-flag rollout — see CLAUDE.md §4.5.1 for taxonomy.

# PR 11+ — Phase 2 model upgrade (Sonnet 4.6 → Opus 4.7) + adaptive thinking
# + max effort on the cohort callsites. Default-ON in dev for parity with
# the production posture (the production env sets the same flag).
AI_PHASE_2_ENABLED=1

# PR 3.2+ — Phase 3 agent-loop primitive. Default-ON in dev so multi-tool
# data-scanning is exercised on every dev mapping run.
AI_PHASE_3_ENABLED=1

# PR 3.4cd commit 4 — Multi-agent mapping pipeline (Generator voted ×3,
# Cross-Table specialist, Cardinality specialist, Critic voted ×3,
# Generator refinement). Default-ON in dev per founder directive
# (overrides the Phase A recommendation of "default OFF until cohort
# eval validates lift" — strategic priority is mapping accuracy and
# consistency in active development; any cost/latency tradeoff
# observed in dev is acceptable while iterating).
#
# Cost implication: under multi-agent the per-pair cost ranges $3-15
# (vs. ~$0.05 single-shot Phase 2). Phase A §I3 estimates $66-910 per
# migration depending on table count. Dev runs against synthetic
# fixtures stay under $20 per run.
AI_PHASE_3_MULTI_AGENT_ENABLED=0
